    <Folder>
      <name>Phu Quoc</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phu Quoc</name>
        <styleUrl>#place-anchor</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b><br/>South<br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.2899,103.984&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.2899, 103.984]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.984,10.2899,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Hotels</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sheraton Phu Quoc Long Beach Resort</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-hotels-t5</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Long Beach, Ganh Dau<br/>5 stars<br/>$97-$200/night <i>(indicative, checked 2026-08-16)</i><br/><br/>A large Marriott-chain beachfront resort on Long Beach with multiple pools, several restaurants and direct sand access.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> Officially rated 5-star with an international chain standard, and its entry-level rooms stay under the trip's price cap despite the brand<br/><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g12666019-d8774806-Reviews-Sheraton_Phu_Quoc_Long_Beach_Resort-Ganh_Dau_Phu_Quoc_Island_Kien_Giang_Province.html">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.momondo.com/hotels/phu-quoc/Sheraton-Phu-Quoc-Long-Beach-Resort.mhd2449378.ksp">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.3375473,103.8498843&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.3375473, 103.8498843]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.8498843,10.3375473,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>L'Azure Resort and Spa</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-hotels-t4</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Duong Dong<br/>4 stars<br/>$63-$115/night <i>(indicative, checked 2026-08-16)</i><br/><br/>A small rustic-eco resort with a private sand beach, pool and spa, officially rated 4-star, built around a low-rise, garden-heavy design rather than a tower.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> Officially rated 4-star with a 9.4-9.5 guest score, and the most consistently well-reviewed 4-star in the pool<br/><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g1184679-d640629-Reviews-L_Azure_Resort_and_Spa-Duong_Dong_Phu_Quoc_Island_Kien_Giang_Province.html">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.makemytrip.com/hotels-international/vietnam/phu_quoc-hotels/l_azure_resort_and_spa-details.html">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.2080717,103.9616615&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.2080717, 103.9616615]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.9616615,10.2080717,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AVS Hotel Phu Quoc</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-hotels-t4</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Duong Dong, 100m from the beach<br/>4 stars<br/>$46-$156/night <i>(indicative, checked 2026-08-16)</i><br/><br/>A modern mid-size hotel a hundred metres from the beach, officially rated 4-star, with a pool, spa and airport transfers.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> Officially rated 4-star, ranked in the top 20 hotels on the island by guest reviews despite its budget-adjacent price<br/><a href="https://en.planetofhotels.com/vietnam/phu-quoc/avs-hotel-phu-quoc">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g1184679-d20200026-Reviews-AVS_Hotel_Phu_Quoc-Duong_Dong_Phu_Quoc_Island_Kien_Giang_Province.html">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.2007569,103.9638791&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.2007569, 103.9638791]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.9638791,10.2007569,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Must-see</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Hon Thom Cable Car</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-must_see</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; An Thoi, southern Phu Quoc<br/><br/>A three-cable gondola line running almost 8 km from the An Thoi coast over open sea to Hon Thom island, in 30-passenger cabins over a 15-minute ride, passing above two smaller islands en route.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> Guinness World Record holder for the longest three-wire sea-crossing cable car, and the way most visitors reach Hon Thom's Sun World park<br/><a href="https://blog.premierresidencesphuquoc.com/hon-thom-cable-car/">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.vietjetair.com/en/news/travel-guides-1665635013747/hon-thom-phu-quoc-cable-car-review-the-worlds-longest-sea-crossing-cable-car-1768878737803">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Hon+Thom+Cable+Car+Phu+Quoc+Vietnam" style="color:#cc0000;font-weight:700">Search YouTube</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=9.9920077,104.0124425&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 9.9920077, 104.0124425]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>104.0124425,9.9920077,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Attractions &amp; Experiences</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Vinpearl Safari Phu Quoc</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-attractions</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Bai Dai, northwest Phu Quoc<br/><i>Approximate location — search the name in Maps</i><br/><br/>Vietnam's largest wildlife conservation park, home to roughly 4,500 animals across 200 species including Bengal tigers, African lions, giraffes and white rhinos, viewable from a safari-style drive-through zone and walking areas.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> The largest wildlife park in the country, and a full-day option that doesn't require a beach or a boat<br/><a href="https://vinwonders.com/en/wonderpedia/news/review-of-vinpearl-safari-phu-quoc/">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g469418-d9748314-Reviews-Vinpearl_Safari_Phu_Quoc-Phu_Quoc_Island_Kien_Giang_Province.html">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Vinpearl+Safari+Phu+Quoc+Phu+Quoc+Vietnam" style="color:#cc0000;font-weight:700">Search YouTube</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.3393964,103.8950113&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.3393964, 103.8950113]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.8950113,10.3393964,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Markets &amp; Shopping</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Phu Quoc Night Market (Dinh Cau)</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-markets</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Duong Dong, Bach Dang street<br/><i>Approximate location — search the name in Maps</i><br/><br/>A single-street night market where diners pick live fish, crab or squid from tanks to be grilled or steamed to order, alongside stalls selling herring salad, banh xeo pancakes and grilled scallops.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> The island's main after-dark food destination since its 2016 merger with the old Dinh Cau market, and the best single stop for trying local seafood specialties in one place<br/><a href="https://www.baconismagic.ca/vietnam/phu-quoc-night-market/">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://vinwonders.com/en/wonderpedia/news/phu-quoc-night-market/">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.3242259,103.8581673&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.3242259, 103.8581673]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.8581673,10.3242259,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>Logistics</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Grab and taxi from Phu Quoc International Airport</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-logistics</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Phu Quoc International Airport (PQC), about 10 km south of Duong Dong<br/><br/>Grab and metered taxis both operate from the terminal; a ride to the Long Beach hotel strip takes about 10-15 minutes and costs roughly 100,000-200,000 VND, with Grab typically 10-20% cheaper than the metered taxi rate.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> The airport sits close enough to the main hotel strip that a transfer is short and cheap regardless of which resort is booked<br/><a href="https://www.airporttransferportal.com/airport-guides/pqc/cost-to-city">source 1</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.grab.com/global/airport-rides/phu-quoc-international-airport/">source 2</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.1727084,103.9921557&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.1727084, 103.9921557]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>103.9921557,10.1727084,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Speedboat from the Mekong Delta (Ha Tien)</name>
        <styleUrl>#s-phu-quoc-logistics</styleUrl>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Phu Quoc</b> &middot; Ha Tien to Bai Vong pier, Phu Quoc<br/><br/>Fast boats from Ha Tien on the Mekong Delta coast to Phu Quoc's Bai Vong pier run 3-5 times daily between about 6am and 2pm, taking roughly 1.5 hours; slower car ferries take about 3 hours on the same route.<br/><b>Why it's here:</b> Connects a Mekong Delta stop directly to Phu Quoc without backtracking through Ho Chi Minh City for a flight<br/><a href="https://www.vietnamcoracle.com/phu-quoc-island-ferry-times/">source 1</a><br/><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=10.1457488,104.038743&travelmode=driving" style="color:#0f7c5c;font-weight:700">Directions</a><br/>Coords: 10.1457488, 104.038743]]></description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>104.038743,10.1457488,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
